      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "observed.sink_ptr_starts_at_copied_command_buffer_end",
      "fine_trace_step": 14,
      "description": "AddressSanitizer-observed sink. On the failing fallback iteration `ptr` already equals `rawmseg + sizeofcmds`, so converting `ptr->cmdsize` performs a 4-byte load from the first byte past the 3028-byte heap buffer and trips the saved heap-buffer-overflow in `get_ne32`."
